Description: An automated surveillance system that detects aberrations in
    laboratory-confirmed infections across all pathogens, presents them to a
    small board of epidemiologists as a ranked list of dossiers, records
    their formal assessment with a full audit trail, and produces outbreak
    reports for clinical colleagues. Statistical outbreak detection uses the
    improved Farrington algorithm of Noufaily et al. (2013)
    <doi:10.1002/sim.5595>, itself an extension of Farrington et al. (1996)
    <doi:10.2307/2983331>, via the 'surveillance' package of Salmon,
    Schumacher, and Hoehle (2016) <doi:10.18637/jss.v070.i10>. Time-varying
    effective reproduction numbers use the method of Cori et al. (2013)
    <doi:10.1093/aje/kwt133> as implemented in 'EpiEstim'. Seasonal epidemic
    thresholds use the Moving Epidemic Method of Vega et al. (2013)
    <doi:10.1111/j.1750-2659.2012.00422.x>. Ships with a synthetic demo data
    set so the whole system can be run without access to any Certe
    infrastructure.
